        {
          "id": "hornsby2021e2-q16b3",
          "type": "mc",
          "stem": "Hence, show that \\(\\displaystyle\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\dfrac{1}{1+k\\sin x}\\,dx=\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{1-k^{2}}}\\tan^{-1}\\sqrt{\\dfrac{1-k}{1+k}}\\), where \\(0<k<1\\).",
          "difficulty": "hard",
          "options": [
            "\\(\\begin{aligned}&\\sin x=\\dfrac{2t}{1+t^{2}},\\ dx=\\dfrac{2\\,dt}{1+t^{2}},\\ t:0\\to1\\\\ &\\int_{0}^{1}\\dfrac{2\\,dt}{t^{2}+2kt+1}=\\int_{0}^{1}\\dfrac{2\\,dt}{(t+k)^{2}+(1-k^{2})}=\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{1-k^{2}}}\\left[\\tan^{-1}\\dfrac{t+k}{\\sqrt{1-k^{2}}}\\right]_{0}^{1}\\\\ &=\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{1-k^{2}}}\\tan^{-1}\\sqrt{\\dfrac{1-k}{1+k}}\\quad\\text{(using }\\tan(A-B)\\text{ on the two arctans)}\\end{aligned}\\)",
            "\\(\\begin{aligned}&\\sin x=\\dfrac{2t}{1+t^{2}},\\ dx=\\dfrac{dt}{1+t^{2}},\\ t:0\\to1\\\\ &\\int_{0}^{1}\\dfrac{dt}{t^{2}+2kt+1}=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{1-k^{2}}}\\left[\\tan^{-1}\\dfrac{t+k}{\\sqrt{1-k^{2}}}\\right]_{0}^{1}\\end{aligned}\\)",
            "\\(\\begin{aligned}&\\sin x=\\dfrac{2t}{1+t^{2}},\\ dx=\\dfrac{2\\,dt}{1+t^{2}},\\ t:0\\to\\infty\\\\ &\\int_{0}^{\\infty}\\dfrac{2\\,dt}{t^{2}+2kt+1}\\end{aligned}\\)",
            "\\(\\begin{aligned}&\\sin x=\\dfrac{1-t^{2}}{1+t^{2}},\\ dx=\\dfrac{2\\,dt}{1+t^{2}}\\\\ &\\int_{0}^{1}\\dfrac{2\\,dt}{1+t^{2}+k(1-t^{2})}\\end{aligned}\\)"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "hint": "Use \\(t=\\tan\\dfrac{x}{2}\\): \\(\\sin x=\\dfrac{2t}{1+t^{2}}\\) and \\(dx=\\dfrac{2\\,dt}{1+t^{2}}\\) (parts (i),(ii)). Limits: \\(x=0\\Rightarrow t=0\\); \\(x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\Rightarrow t=\\tan\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}=1\\). Then complete the square in the denominator.",
          "steps": [
            {
              "explain": "Substitute: \\(1+k\\sin x=\\dfrac{1+t^{2}+2kt}{1+t^{2}}\\); multiply by \\(dx=\\dfrac{2\\,dt}{1+t^{2}}\\): the \\((1+t^{2})\\) cancels.",
              "work": "\\(\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\dfrac{dx}{1+k\\sin x}=\\int_{0}^{1}\\dfrac{2\\,dt}{t^{2}+2kt+1}\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Complete the square: \\(t^{2}+2kt+1=(t+k)^{2}+(1-k^{2})\\), where \\(1-k^{2}>0\\) because \\(0<k<1\\). Let \\(s^{2}=1-k^{2}\\).",
              "work": "\\(=\\int_{0}^{1}\\dfrac{2\\,dt}{(t+k)^{2}+s^{2}}=\\dfrac{2}{s}\\left[\\tan^{-1}\\dfrac{t+k}{s}\\right]_{0}^{1}\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Evaluate: \\(\\dfrac{2}{s}\\left[\\tan^{-1}\\dfrac{1+k}{s}-\\tan^{-1}\\dfrac{k}{s}\\right]\\). Use \\(\\tan(A-B)=\\dfrac{\\tan A-\\tan B}{1+\\tan A\\tan B}\\).",
              "work": "\\(\\tan(A-B)=\\dfrac{\\dfrac{1+k}{s}-\\dfrac{k}{s}}{1+\\dfrac{k(1+k)}{s^{2}}}=\\dfrac{\\dfrac{1}{s}}{\\dfrac{1-k^{2}+k+k^{2}}{s^{2}}}=\\dfrac{s}{1+k}\\)"
